From: Xie Bo <xb@ultrarisc.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:15:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] RISC-V: KVM: Propagate interrupted G-stage faults
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.55
Git-commit: f41fb17143df890855d3de980f8eb92dfd595817

commit f41fb17143df890855d3de980f8eb92dfd595817 upstream.

__kvm_faultin_pfn() reports an interrupted host page fault with
KVM_PFN_ERR_SIGPENDING. RISC-V currently handles it as a generic
error PFN and returns -EFAULT.

Return -EINTR for the signal-pending sentinel so callers can distinguish
an interrupted fault from an invalid userspace mapping. Do not log the
expected interruption as a vCPU exit error.

Fixes: 9d05c1fee837 ("RISC-V: KVM: Implement stage2 page table programming")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Xie Bo <xb@ultrarisc.com>
Reviewed-by: Anup Patel <anup@brainfault.org>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260810051544.3953925-3-xb@ultrarisc.com
Signed-off-by: Anup Patel <anup@brainfault.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 arch/riscv/kvm/mmu.c       | 2 ++
 arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_exit.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/kvm/mmu.c b/arch/riscv/kvm/mmu.c
index 58f5f3536ffd..b5a809a091d6 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/mmu.c
@@ -380,6 +380,8 @@ int kvm_riscv_mmu_map(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct kvm_memory_slot *memslot,
 				vma_pageshift, current);
 		return 0;
 	}
+	if (is_sigpending_pfn(hfn))
+		return -EINTR;
 	if (is_error_noslot_pfn(hfn))
 		return -EFAULT;
 
diff --git a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_exit.c b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_exit.c
index 0bb0c51e3c89..219f553cc2b7 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_exit.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_exit.c
@@ -248,7 +248,7 @@ int kvm_riscv_vcpu_exit(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct kvm_run *run,
 	}
 
 	/* Print details in-case of error */
-	if (ret < 0) {
+	if (ret < 0 && ret != -EINTR) {
 		kvm_err("VCPU exit error %d\n", ret);
 		kvm_err("SEPC=0x%lx SSTATUS=0x%lx HSTATUS=0x%lx\n",
 			vcpu->arch.guest_context.sepc,
-- 
2.53.0

